  "description": "The size limits of a shdccp/2 stream (RFC 07 sections 4.4 and 6.6, P8): the rank coder's codes at their largest (25 bits for an escape after 255 candidates, which needs more than one chunk; 23 bits within a 720-byte chunk), the bits used before padding, and the streams of records of 1, 720, 721, 59,760 and 60,000 bytes of a high-cost text. Residuals and streams come from Owl's encodeChunk and growBiochain; code lengths from cv_spec.mjs, checked against them. informative.stream_bound is the bound of section 4.4 for the record's n bytes (377,016 hex digits for 60,000 bytes; cap_hex, 84 x 4,524 = 380,016, is the bound for any 84 frames): arithmetic on the section's formula, which no independent implementation computes, so it is not an expected value.",
